Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:27:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 070/112] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7250-motorola-nairo: Set the
 Wi-Fi calibration variant

The WCN3990 reports board ID 0xff, so ath10k fell back to generic board
data (regulatory domain 0x406c, every 5 GHz channel passive). Name the
board so that the board-2.bin entry built from Motorola's own board data
(bdwlan_nairo_<variant>.bin, picked per radio as Android's cnss-daemon
does) is found as variant=motorola_nairo.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
index 5efe077bc..51a87cb56 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
@@ -569,5 +569,7 @@ &wifi {
 	vdd-3.3-ch0-supply = <&vreg_l10c_3p3>;
 	vdd-3.3-ch1-supply = <&vreg_l11c_3p3>;
 
+	qcom,calibration-variant = "motorola_nairo";
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
